---
import BlogPostLayout from "../../layouts/BlogPostLayout.astro";
import BlogByline from "../../components/BlogByline.astro";
import { PRICING, CHECKLIST, POLICIES, TRUST } from "../../data/claims";

const publishDate = '2026-09-01';
const modifiedDate = '2026-09-01';
const readTime = '5 min read';

const petFee = `$${POLICIES.pets.feePerPet}`;
const shedFee = `+$${POLICIES.pets.heavyShedSurcharge}`;

// FAQ: single source of truth — BlogPostLayout emits the FAQPage schema from
// this array. The visible FAQ section below renders from the same array.
const faqs = [
  {
    question: "Do you charge extra for pets?",
    answer: `Yes. ${petFee} per pet. Heavy shedding is ${shedFee}. Both are on our pricing page.`
  },
  {
    question: "Can you get dog smell out?",
    answer: "Surface smell, often. Pad and duct smell, not with a regular clean. We will tell you if the job you want is not the job we sell."
  },
  {
    question: "Are your products safe if a dog licks the floor?",
    answer: "We use pet-safe products and can run unscented. Floors should be dry before a pet is back on them. That is normal."
  },
  {
    question: "Do I need to leave?",
    answer: `No. A lot of clients leave a code. Teams are background-checked and insured for ${TRUST.liabilityCoverageDisplay}.`
  }
];
---

<BlogPostLayout
  title={`Pet Hair Cleaning: ${petFee} per Pet, ${shedFee} for Heavy Shed | Valley Clean Team`}
  schemaTitle="Pet Hair Cleaning"
  description={`What we charge for pets, what the ${shedFee} heavy-shed fee is for, and what a regular visit will and will not fix when the house has dogs or cats.`}
  publishDate={publishDate}
  modifiedDate={modifiedDate}
  faqs={faqs}
>

  <!-- Hero Section -->
  <section class="pt-32 pb-16 px-6 bg-gradient-to-br from-[#1a1a2e] via-[#16213e] to-[#0f3460]">
    <div class="container mx-auto max-w-4xl">
      <div class="text-center">
        <span class="inline-block px-4 py-2 bg-[#FFA985]/20 text-[#FFA985] rounded-full text-sm font-semibold mb-6">
          Pet Care
        </span>
        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-bold mb-6 text-white leading-tight">
          Pet Hair <span class="text-[#FFA985]">Cleaning</span>
        </h1>
        <div class="mb-8">
          <BlogByline variant="dark" date={publishDate} readTime={readTime} />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Article Content -->
  <article class="py-16 px-6">
    <div class="container mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">

        <p class="text-xl text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-8">
          Pets are fine. We clean houses with dogs and cats every week. The published fees are <strong>{petFee} per pet</strong> and <strong>{shedFee} when shedding is heavy</strong>. Pet-safe products are the default. <a href="/services/green-cleaning" class="text-[#FFA985] font-semibold hover:underline">Green or fragrance-free</a> is available at no extra product charge.
        </p>

        <p>
          Regular cleaning still starts at <strong>{PRICING.regular.display}</strong>. Deep cleaning still starts at <strong>{PRICING.deep.display}</strong>. Those fees sit on top of the visit price. Full list: <a href="/pricing" class="text-[#FFA985] font-semibold hover:underline">pricing</a>.
        </p>

        <p>
          Call <a href="tel:2568261100" class="text-[#FFA985] font-semibold hover:underline">256-826-1100</a> or <a href="/request-a-quote" class="text-[#FFA985] font-semibold hover:underline">request a quote</a>. Tell us the animals when you book. That is how the invoice stays honest.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-[#333333] mt-12 mb-6">What the two pet fees are for</h2>

        <p>
          <strong>{petFee} per pet</strong> is the standard add-on. Hair on baseboards, furniture edges, and floors takes extra passes. One lab is not the same job as a house with no animals.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>{shedFee} heavy shed</strong> is for the visit where hair is a layer, not a dusting. Under the couch, in the vents you can see, packed in corners, stuck to the baseboards after a seasonal blowout. It is not a punishment fee. It is time.
        </p>

        <p>
          We would rather say the {shedFee} on the call than send a team into a two-hour overrun and invent a line item at the door.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-[#333333] mt-12 mb-6">What a regular visit will do</h2>

        <p>
          On the {CHECKLIST.standard}-item <a href="/services/regular-cleaning" class="text-[#FFA985] font-semibold hover:underline">regular clean</a>:
        </p>

        <ul class="space-y-3 mb-8">
          <li>Floors vacuumed and mopped</li>
          <li>Furniture we can move safely around, not a full lift-and-extract of every sofa</li>
          <li>Hair pulled off reachable baseboards and corners</li>
          <li>Kitchen and bath as usual</li>
          <li>Trash out</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          A regular visit is maintenance. It keeps hair from becoming the room. It does not replace a carpet extractor or an upholstery shop.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-[#333333] mt-12 mb-6">What it will not do</h2>

        <ul class="space-y-3 mb-8">
          <li>Pull hair out of every couch cushion on a regular stop</li>
          <li>Wash the dog bed unless you add laundry</li>
          <li>Deodorize with a fogger or ozone machine</li>
          <li>Guarantee a house will smell like it has no pets</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          If the smell is in the carpet pad or the HVAC, cleaning the surfaces will not finish the job. Say that on the call if that is the real problem.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-[#333333] mt-12 mb-6">When to book a deep clean instead</h2>

        <p>
          Book <a href="/services/deep-cleaning" class="text-[#FFA985] font-semibold hover:underline">deep cleaning</a> from {PRICING.deep.display} when hair has had months to settle: baseboards, fans, the backs of doors, the kitchen kick plates, the spare room nobody uses.
        </p>

        <p>
          After that, weekly or biweekly regular visits keep it from returning to that state. Weekly is the better fit for two shedders and kids. The schedule math is here: <a href="/blog/weekly-vs-biweekly-house-cleaning" class="text-[#FFA985] font-semibold hover:underline">weekly vs biweekly</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-[#333333] mt-12 mb-6">Products and allergies</h2>

        <p>
          We do not use a separate “pet formula” as a surprise upcharge. Pet-safe is standard. If someone in the house has asthma or hates fragrance, ask for unscented. There is no product surcharge for that.
        </p>

        <p>
          If you need us to skip a room because a reactive animal is crated there, say so when you book. We work around closed doors.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-[#333333] mt-12 mb-6">How to make the visit count</h2>

        <ul class="space-y-3 mb-8">
          <li>Pick up toys, leashes, and food bowls off the floor</li>
          <li>Crate or walk the animal if they shadow the vacuum</li>
          <li>Tell us about a cat that hides in the guest-room closet</li>
          <li>Mention a recent blowout or a new puppy</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          We can clean with the pet home. A nervous dog in the hallway slows the job and is not safer for the animal.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-[#333333] mt-12 mb-6">Frequently asked questions</h2>

        {faqs.map((faq) => (
          <>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#333333] mt-6 mb-3">{faq.question}</h3>
            <p>{faq.answer}</p>
          </>
        ))}

      </div>

      <!-- CTA Section -->
      <div class="mt-16 p-8 bg-gradient-to-br from-[#FFA985]/10 to-[#FFC67D]/10 rounded-2xl border border-[#FFA985]/20 text-center">
        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-[#333333] mb-4">Get a number that includes the pets</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-600 mb-6">Do not wait until we are in the driveway to mention the shepherd. Put it on the quote.</p>
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
          <a href="tel:2568261100" class="btn-primary px-8 py-4 rounded-lg font-semibold inline-flex items-center justify-center">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 mr-2" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M3 5a2 2 0 012-2h3.28a1 1 0 01.948.684l1.498 4.493a1 1 0 01-.502 1.21l-2.257 1.13a11.042 11.042 0 005.516 5.516l1.13-2.257a1 1 0 011.21-.502l4.493 1.498a1 1 0 01.684.949V19a2 2 0 01-2 2h-1C9.716 21 3 14.284 3 6V5z"></path></svg>
            Get your price — 256-826-1100
          </a>
          <a href="/request-a-quote" class="bg-white border-2 border-[#FFA985] text-[#333333] px-8 py-4 rounded-lg font-semibold hover:bg-[#FFA985]/10 transition inline-flex items-center justify-center">
            Request a quote online
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="text-gray-600 mt-6">Tennessee: <a href="tel:6155101427" class="text-[#FFA985] font-semibold hover:underline">615-510-1427</a></p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

</BlogPostLayout>
